    "id": "p19-q11-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "11",
    "prompt": "From a class of 14 students, a teacher forms three groups of sizes 6, 5, and 3. How many such groupings are possible?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$168\\,168$",
      "worked": "Choose the group of six, then the group of five from the eight remaining students. The remaining three form the last group. Different group sizes distinguish the groups.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N&=\\binom{14}{6}\\binom{8}{5}\\binom{3}{3}\\\\N&=3003\\times56\\times1\\\\N&=168\\,168.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
